  "verbalization": "Cis-Dehydrocurvularin is implicated in the biological pathway leading to FaDu through a series of molecular interactions. The drug is directly linked to SN12K1, which is a target of multiple compounds, including 5,16-Dimethoxy-10-methyl-10-azatricyclo[11.4.0.02,7]heptadeca-1(13),2,4,6,14,16-hexaen-4-ol and (1R,2S,4R,7S,11R,14R,16S)-16-(dimethylamino)-8-propan-2-ylidene-14-prop-1-en-2-yl-3,6,15-trioxatetracyclo[9.3.1.14,7.02,4]hexadecane-5,9,12-trione. All these compounds are ultimately targeted by FaDu, suggesting a shared biological function or pathway. The presence of multiple targets for SN12K1, along with the direct link to FaDu, indicates that Cis-Dehydrocurvularin may act through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of SN12K1, which in turn influences FaDu. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Cis-Dehydrocurvularin in regulating the expression or function of FaDu through a series of molecular intermediates.",
